From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:04:18 +0100
Subject: drm/lima: cancel a pending heap recovery in the timeout handler

An out-of-heap interrupt queues pipe->recover_work. If the job then
fails for another reason (an MMU page fault or the scheduler timeout)
before the work runs, the timeout handler resets the core and clears
pipe->current_task, and the work later runs lima_gp_task_recover() on
the idle core: it dereferences the NULL current_task and restarts the
PLBU allocation of a job that no longer exists.

After masking the irqs, disable the work until the reset is done. This
cancels a queued recovery and waits for a running one; a running one
unmasks the GP irqs and restarts the PLBU, so mask the irqs again and
wait for an irq handler that may still be running. Its schedule_work()
now fails instead of queueing a recovery that would run after the
reset. Enable the work again once current_task is cleared.

Found by review; this race has not been observed on hardware.

Fixes: 2081e8dcf1ee ("drm/lima: recover task by enlarging heap buffer")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c | 15 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
@@ -434,6 +434,18 @@ static enum drm_gpu_sched_stat lima_sched_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *job
 	 */
 	pipe->task_mask_irq(pipe);
 
+	/*
+	 * A heap recovery queued before the error must not run on the reset
+	 * core. Disable it until the reset is done: this cancels a queued
+	 * recovery and waits for a running one. A running one unmasks the GP
+	 * irqs again, so mask them once more and wait for an irq handler that
+	 * may still be running; its schedule_work() now fails.
+	 */
+	disable_work_sync(&pipe->recover_work);
+	pipe->task_mask_irq(pipe);
+	for (i = 0; i < pipe->num_processor; i++)
+		synchronize_irq(pipe->processor[i]->irq);
+
 	if (!pipe->error)
 		DRM_ERROR("%s job timeout\n", lima_ip_name(ip));
 
@@ -464,6 +476,9 @@ static enum drm_gpu_sched_stat lima_sched_timedout_job(struct drm_sched_job *job
 	pipe->current_vm = NULL;
 	pipe->current_task = NULL;
 
+	/* nothing left to recover on the reset core */
+	enable_work(&pipe->recover_work);
+
 	lima_pm_idle(ldev);
 
 	drm_sched_resubmit_jobs(&pipe->base);
-- 
